# Everything published here is hashed by third parties over its exact bytes, and an anchored
# digest is permanent. Git's newline translation would make a file's hash depend on the OS that
# checked it out, so a Windows contributor and a Linux verifier would compute different digests
# for a byte-identical archive. Caught 2026-08-12: signature.json was 603 bytes locally with
# CRLF and 591 bytes on GitHub with LF, so digests.txt recorded a hash nobody else could
# reproduce. Turn translation off for the whole tree.
* -text

# Belt and braces for the files whose bytes are actually signed or digested.
snapshots/** -text
digests.txt -text
index-pubkey.json -text
